            {
              "id": "cc41f525-ab6e-42cc-aee7-d23596d28c84",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Digital Leisure, the Internet &amp; Popular Culture: Communities &amp; Identities in a Digital Age</strong></em> was written by Karl Spracklen, published by Palgrave Macmillan, May 28, 2015."
            },
            {
              "id": "a2e87c0f-8560-45ab-a504-38670d4c85ad",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "bf378edf-bf24-4610-bdf2-403749523ea2",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Spracklen explores the impact of the internet on leisure and leisure studies, examining the ways in which digital leisure spaces and activities have become part of everyday leisure. Covering a range of issues from social media and file-sharing to romance on the Internet, this book presents new theoretical directions for digital leisure.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "cbfabc5c-0378-435e-a763-7e9ed3b5cef3",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
